# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Most source files carry an `SPDX-License-Identifier:` line, and that line is
# authoritative for the file it stands in. A number of files CANNOT carry one:
#   * generated files, whose generator would have to emit the line as well,
#   * files that are inlined verbatim into a generated file,
#   * files whose line 1 is a test directive the test runner reads
#     (`// expect_exit:`, `// expect_out:`, `// expect_error:`, `// expect_ok`),
#   * symbolic links, which have no content of their own.
# This file assigns a licence to those too, by path, so that every single file
# in the repository has an answer. The reasoning is in LICENSING.md; the full
# texts are in LICENSE (GPL-2.0-only) and LICENSE.MIT.

